{
 "notes": [
  "BUTTON CONFIG (original scene 16: init 0x28329, list 0x28189, draw 0x27d74, exit 0x280ed; bars 0x1dd658, labels 0x1dd7e0, markers 0x1dd558, arrows 0x1dd968 at 0x1dd9f4, help strings 0x1dda24).",
  "Up and down move the cursor, wrapping on a new press. On a choice row left and right flip its value (wrapping). On an action's row the first assignable button pressed (A, B, X, Y, L, R, white, black, in that order) is assigned to the action, and the action that had it takes the row's old button, silently.",
  "Confirm on DEFAULT restores the default assignments only; on EXIT it fades out to exit_to, keeping everything. There is no cancel: B is an assignable button.",
  "The selected row's bar replaces its dimmed one and pulses throughout. A choice row shows its arrows while selected; an action's row shows the marker of its button on the controller picture.",
  "The help lines are the original's, including BEGINNER MODE's, which ends with EXIT's text."
 ],
